To find the intersection of sets A and B (A ∩ B) after the end of the third revision r3, we need to identify the elements that are common to both sets in that revision.

In the 3rd revision r3:
- A = {1, 4, 5, 6}
- B = {2, 5}

The intersection of A and B (A ∩ B) in r3 is the set of elements that are in both A and B. In this case, the only element that is in both sets is 5.

Therefore, A ∩ B after the end of the third revision r3 is {5}.

